"The patient underwent a robot-assisted radical prostatectomy with a pathological stage of pT3a, Gleason 4+3 (ISUP grade group 3), and positive surgical margins. The seminal vesicles were not invaded, and lymphovascular invasion was absent, with no lymph node metastasis documented. The preoperative PSA was 16.5. The surgical findings, including positive margins and the Gleason grade, are significant factors in the prognosis. The absence of lymph node metastasis is a favorable finding.\n\nThe biopsy grade was Gleason 4+3 (ISUP grade group 3), which aligns with the prostatectomy specimen. The extent of disease, pT3a without extraprostatic extension, and positive margins are concerning elements. Missing postoperative PSA or follow-up information widens the uncertainty regarding the subsequent trajectory. The nodal status is documented as no lymph node metastasis. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory would be crucial to revise the prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 41.66 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 31.24–52.07 months; its coverage has not been validated."
